Chapter: BloomSpread
  cites Foreword chapter BloomFilter

 The bit position is a remainder, so it reads the LOW bits. That makes
 the modulus decisive: 1024 is a power of two and reads the low bits
 alone, while 1021 is prime and samples the whole word. A defect can
 hide entirely in the second. Both are here for that reason.

 100 inserted, 500 queried, disjoint by construction, k=4. At m/n of
 about 10 the textbook rate is near 1 per cent, so single digits per
 500 is healthy. The fill percentages are the control: if two runs set
 the same fraction of bits, a difference in false positives is about
 WHERE the bits landed and not how many.

Section: Integer keys

  fill-int : BloomFilter, Integer, Integer -> BloomFilter
  fill-int (bf) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then bf
    else fill-int (bloom-add bf (i * 7919)) (i + 1) n

  fp-int : BloomFilter, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fp-int (bf) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else fp-int bf (i + 1) n (acc + (if bloom-contains bf (1000000 + i * 7919) then 1 else 0))

  run-int : Integer -> Integer
  run-int (m) = fp-int (fill-int (bloom-new m 4) 0 100) 0 500 0

  fill-pct : Integer -> Integer
  fill-pct (m) = bloom-false-positive-rate (fill-int (bloom-new m 4) 0 100)

Section: Text keys

  fill-text : BloomFilter, Integer, Integer -> BloomFilter
  fill-text (bf) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then bf
    else fill-text (bloom-add-text bf (show (i * 7919))) (i + 1) n

  fp-text : BloomFilter, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fp-text (bf) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else fp-text bf (i + 1) n (acc + (if bloom-contains-text bf (show (1000000 + i * 7919)) then 1 else 0))

  run-text : Integer -> Integer
  run-text (m) = fp-text (fill-text (bloom-new m 4) 0 100) 0 500 0

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("fp-int-1024=" & show (run-int 1024))
    print-line-uni ("fp-int-1021=" & show (run-int 1021))
    print-line-uni ("fill-pct-1024=" & show (fill-pct 1024))
    print-line-uni ("fill-pct-1021=" & show (fill-pct 1021))
    print-line-uni ("fp-text-1024=" & show (run-text 1024))
    print-line-uni ("fp-text-1021=" & show (run-text 1021))
  end

